    "notes": "\"Historical Returns on Stocks, Bonds and Bills\" (histretSP), sheet \"Returns by year\", 1928-2025, copied without adjustment. sha256 is of the raw workbook. TIMING: calendar year, end of December to end of December (unlike shiller-annual.json, which is January-average to January-average), nominal, decimals. sp500: (year-end index - prior year-end index + dividends during the year) / prior year-end index; dividends are not reinvested within the year. tBill3m: average 3-month T-bill rate during the year, used directly as the year's return. tBond10y: constant-maturity 10-year Treasury; coupon at the prior year-end yield plus the price change of a 10-year par bond repriced at the new year-end yield with the maturity kept at 10 years. baaCorporate: same construction applied to Moody's Baa corporate yield. inflation: CPI-U (not seasonally adjusted) calendar-year change as published in the sheet. Used as a cross-check on shiller-annual.json and as a corporate-bond series for Trinity-style comparisons (the Trinity study itself used Ibbotson long-term high-grade corporates, which this Baa series only approximates)."
